# BUILD_linux is BUILD plus ONE change: the VER08b runtime-capability line runs with
# RCG_STRICT=1.  The build tool picks BUILD_linux first on Linux, BUILD on macOS
# (BUILD_mac / BUILD_mac_and_linux do not exist here) and BUILD_windows on Windows.
# KEEP THE REST OF THIS FILE IN SYNC WITH BUILD.
cargo test -q -p logic-gates --lib -- --nocapture
cargo test -q -p logic-gates --doc
cargo test -q -p logic-gates --test gates_test --test combinational_test --test sequential_test --test bit_domain --test decoder_width
# SEC-007: the bit domain is also checked in the RELEASE profile, where the crate's own
# validation used to be compiled away (a debug-only `debug_assert!`).  The same file passes
# in both profiles or the build fails.
cargo test -q -p logic-gates --release --test bit_domain --test decoder_width
# ... and the whole generated Warrant harness (every rejection row included) in release too.
cargo test -q -p logic-gates --release --test warrant_evidence
# The library is pure: no capability, test code included (the analyzer reads it).
cargo run -q -p coding_adventures_ca_capability_analyzer -- --dir .
# VER08b: every public stateless operation (the gates and the combinational blocks) runs
# inside a seccomp/Landlock jail derived from required_capabilities.json (no capabilities),
# watched by an independent strace; RCG_STRICT=1 makes a NOT-LIVE gate a failure.
# The container ring is skipped, not failed, where no Docker daemon is reachable.
RCG_STRICT=1 cargo test -q -p logic-gates --test runtime_capability
# VER04h: the evidence harness is generated from code/specs/logic-gates.warrant and
# evidence.bindings.  Fail if the checked-in file drifted, rewrite the evidence
# manifest from a real run, and prove each sabotage mode makes a model-pinned
# exhaustive suite of each operation report `not ok` (each filter names the cheap
# claim that pins the faulted behaviour; a fault applies to every operation that
# lists it, and the filter selects which operation's claim is attacked).
cargo run -q -p coding_adventures_warrant_grammar --example gen_evidence -- --check logic-gates
